plete. The garden-tool-loan and garden-volunteer-shift workflows (6 of 15 screens) are engine scaffolding wearing a garden label: every screen repeats the identical chip triplet \\\"Details ready / Editable / State saved\\\", the identical helper sentence \\\"This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.\\\", a generic 9-dot grid icon, and complete states whose entire payload is the tautology \\\"Saved -- Garden tool loan state updated.\\\" / \\\"Volunteer shift signup updated.\\\" No tool name, queue position, due date, shift date, time, or slot count is ever shown. Two screens (tool-loan start, export start) are also captured mid-scroll with the primary card's title clipped off above the app bar. Failing on placeholder-grade copy in two of five workflows.\"\n  ,\n  \"holisticQuestionAnswers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"context-state-legibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Across this community's workflows, is it always clear what workflow and what state (start/in-progress/complete) the user is looking at?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Workflow identity is mostly clear -- the green \\\"Garden Club\\\" app bar plus per-card titles (\\\"Spring Planting Workshop\\\", \\\"Basil seedlings offer\\\", \\\"Garden tool loan\\\", \\\"Garden volunteer shift\\\", \\\"Garden data export package\\\") name the workflow on 13 of 15 screens, and modal sheets carry a matching X-titled header (\\\"Spring Workshop\\\", \\\"Offer a plant\\\", \\\"Garden tool loan\\\", \\\"Garden volunteer shift\\\", \\\"Garden export package\\\"). State legibility is where it breaks down. RSVP and plant-exchange read cleanly: \\\"Your RSVP\\\" -> \\\"Choose your response\\\" with a selected \\\"Going\\\" pill -> \\\"Your RSVP: Going\\\" + \\\"RSVP confirmed\\\" + a \\\"Going\\\" check chip; and \\\"Offer plant\\\" -> \\\"Offer plant\\\"/\\\"Edit offer\\\" -> \\\"Offer posted\\\" + \\\"Posted\\\" check chip. But tool-loan and volunteer-shift show the same \\\"Details ready / Editable / State saved\\\" chip row in ALL THREE states, so the start screen already claims \\\"State saved\\\" before anything has been done, and the only real state signal is a small \\\"Saved\\\" chip in the corner. On the export start screen the card title is scrolled off entirely -- the user sees only \\\"Redaction preview / Checksum verified / Download ready / Generate export\\\" floating under the app bar with no heading, and on tool-loan start the card above is sliced through mid-word (\\\"Tap for expanded view\\\" / \\\"Data package\\\" cut in half).\",\n      \"score\": 58,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"On garden-tool-loan start, action, and complete the identical chips 'Details ready', 'Editable', 'State saved' appear -- 'State saved' is shown before the user has done anything\",\n        \"On garden-export-custom-schemas start the topmost visible element is a partial card showing only 'Redaction preview', 'Checksum verified', 'Download ready' and a 'Generate export' button with no title above it\",\n        \"On garden-event-rsvp complete the header block reads 'Your RSVP: Going' with a separate 'RSVP confirmed' panel and a check-marked 'Going' chip, which is unambiguous\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-start\", \"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-action\", \"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-complete\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-start\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-action\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-complete\", \"garden-club-garden-export-custom-schemas-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"copy-accuracy\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the displayed text read like real product copy about actual Garden Club content, or like generic scaffolding?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Split. Three workflows carry copy that could ship: \\\"Hands-on bed prep, seedling swap, and seasonal planning with Garden Club members.\\\", \\\"Offer six Sweet Genovese starter pots, choose pickup details, and control what contact info is shared.\\\", \\\"The package will include event attendance, plant offers, redacted member contact fields, and an audit checksum.\\\" -- all specific to a gardening club, with real nouns and numbers. Two workflows do not: tool-loan and volunteer-shift bodies are engine-narration about the UI itself (\\\"This view shows editable details, current progress, and the next step before saving.\\\", \\\"Task details\\\", \\\"Saved details\\\") plus status strings that restate the workflow name (\\\"Garden tool loan state updated.\\\", \\\"Volunteer shift signup updated.\\\"). The one-line hooks that ARE specific (\\\"Borrow the broadfork and manage the loan queue.\\\", \\\"Compost turning shift has open volunteer slots.\\\") are then repeated verbatim two or three times per screen as title-subtitle-body-and-Task-details, which reads as template filling rather than authored copy.\",\n      \"score\": 52,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"garden-tool-loan complete shows 'Garden tool loan state updated.' three separate times -- as card body, under 'Saved details', and under 'Saved'\",\n        \"garden-volunteer-shift action shows 'Sign up for the compost turning volunteer shift.' as both the card body and again verbatim under the 'Task details' heading\",\n        \"By contrast plant-exchange-submission action shows authored copy: 'Confirm the variety, pickup window, and privacy note before the offer appears on the plant exchange board.'\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-start\", \"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-action\", \"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-complete\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-start\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-action\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-complete\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"visual-quality\",\n      \"question\": \"Is there repeated generic card shell, thin content, clipping, or crowding?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Yes, in the two weak workflows and at two capture boundaries. The tool-loan and volunteer-shift action sheets are pixel-for-pixel the same layout -- same 9-dot grid glyph in a circle, same green hero card, same dark 'This view shows editable details...' strip with 'Edit response', same 'Task details' card with the same three chips, same teal primary button, same low-contrast 'Edit details' link -- differing only in the string substituted into each slot. Their complete screens likewise duplicate each other. The 'Edit details' text on both action sheets is dark teal on a near-black card and is barely legible. There is also visible dead space: the export start screen has roughly a third of the viewport empty below 'Local package details' with only a chevron, and the tool-loan start screen has a similar empty band below the card. The RSVP and plant-exchange screens do not have this problem -- they carry dense, differentiated content (date/time/location/capacity chips, plant variety chips, an 'Offer preview' section).\",\n      \"score\": 55,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"garden-tool-loan action and garden-volunteer-shift action are identical layouts down to the 9-dot grid icon, chip positions, teal 'Start ...' button and faint 'Edit details' link\",\n        \"On both action sheets 'Edit details' renders in dark teal on a dark card, far below normal contrast\",\n        \"garden-export-custom-schemas start has a large empty region between 'Local package details' and the bottom nav bar\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-action\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-action\", \"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-complete\", \"garden-club-garden-volunteer-shift-complete\", \"garden-club-garden-export-custom-schemas-start\", \"garden-club-garden-tool-loan-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"actionability\",\n      \"question\": \"A