king the schedule, location, host, and capacity.') and the single outlined 'RSVP to event' button is the obvious next step. Two blemishes: the blue event card against the green 'Garden Club' app bar and green 'Care and volunteers' card below is the only non-green surface on the screen and reads as an unthemed component, and the bottom of the viewport is crowded -- the 'Plant exchange subm...' card is truncated mid-title and half-hidden behind the nav bar, with the 'Documents' tab label itself clipped at the right screen edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A garden event RSVP entry point with the event named, dated, located, capacity-counted, and an unambiguous un-answered RSVP state -- which this delivers; theming of the event card should follow the community accent, and the card stack should not collide with the bottom nav.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Hero title 'Spring Planting Workshop' with calendar-check icon in a translucent circle\",\n        \"Chips: 'Sat, Apr 18', '10:00 AM', 'Riverside Greenhouse', '18 of 24 spots'\",\n        \"'Your RSVP' panel with instructional body text and no answer selected\",\n        \"Outlined 'RSVP to event' button\",\n        \"Green 'Care and volunteers' card: 'Private requests, volunteer shifts, and member support.'\",\n        \"'Plant exchange subm...' card truncated and partially occluded by the bottom nav; 'Documents' tab label clipped at right edge\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear this is the pre-RSVP start state rather than a completed one?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Your RSVP' followed by 'Choose Going, Maybe, or Not going after checking the schedule, location, host, and capacity.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The panel heading has no value appended and the body is phrased as a forward instruction, so no answer has been given yet. The complete-state screen 